      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Erratic behavior like inconsistent timeouts and spikes is often indicative of upstream network issues rather than a single physical cable failure. While bad hardware can cause drops, repeated timeouts on a specific hop often mean that router is dropping traffic due to overload or is experiencing an intermittent link saturation. I would recommend checking the utilization and interface errors statistics on the device at hop 4, as it's immediately preceding the failure point.",
